 "Any independent poll showing Macy within single digits, or major outside spending entering the district, would signal the race is genuinely tightening.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Ben Cline (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Ben Cline seeks another term in a Shenandoah Valley–anchored district that leaned about twelve points Republican at the presidential level. He faces Beth Macy, a former journalist who has proven a strong fundraiser, slightly outpacing Cline in money and holding a modest cash advantage. National Democrats have publicly labeled the seat 'in play,' and the two have sparred over debates and data centers.\n\nThe available polling, though from a Republican-sponsored firm, shows Cline well ahead among likely voters, and prediction markets price his chances around 93%. The fundamentals still favor the incumbent in a midterm environment that may help Democrats, but the structural lean and lack of independent evidence of a close race make Cline the clear favorite, with Macy needing a significant late shift to contend.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0375, "margin": -14.4}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0463, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0527, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0614, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0472, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0359, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}, {"date